WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.648
After the crushing defeat at Red Cliffs, Cao Cao led his remaining troops in a hurried flight toward the narrow Huarong road.

00:00:06.998 --> 00:00:11.438
The mountain road was muddy and hard to travel; the soldiers were tired and hungry, their steps heavy.

00:00:11.788 --> 00:00:17.596
Zhuge Liang, with his uncanny foresight, had long since sent Guan Yu with troops to wait on the Huarong road.

00:00:17.946 --> 00:00:21.834
Guan Yu held his great blade and quietly watched the end of the mountain road.

00:00:22.184 --> 00:00:27.944
Guan Yu looked at Cao Cao and remembered the kindness of years ago — the gift of a horse and a robe — and his heart could not bear it.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:31.342
On one side was his military order, on the other his debt of gratitude — he was torn between the two.

00:00:31.692 --> 00:00:37.044
He sighed deeply, stepped aside to open the road, and let Cao Cao and his soldiers pass.

00:00:37.394 --> 00:00:40.874
Cao Cao thanked him again and again, and hurried away from the valley with his men.

00:00:41.224 --> 00:00:46.264
Guan Yu returned to camp and of his own accord asked Zhuge Liang for punishment, admitting he had let Cao Cao go.

00:00:46.614 --> 00:00:49.494
He calmly took responsibility, making no excuses for himself.

00:00:49.844 --> 00:00:55.172
Zhuge Liang, valuing Guan Yu's loyalty and sense of honor, smiled and forgave him, and the two smiled at each other.

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:58.354
This story made people remember how precious honor and loyalty are.

